1
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,200
All right.

2
00:01:48,599 --> 00:01:50,319
Since you've made up your minds,

3
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,319
I won't try to keep you.

4
00:01:54,879 --> 00:01:57,400
I'll call Zhong'an's Africa branch

5
00:01:57,959 --> 00:02:00,599
and have them do everything to assist you.

6
00:02:01,359 --> 00:02:02,319
Once you get back,

7
00:02:02,319 --> 00:02:03,680
get in touch with them right away.

8
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,920
Let them know if you run into any trouble.

9
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:08,560
Thank you.

10
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:10,199
All right, thanks.

11
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:13,400
By the way, there's one more thing.

12
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:16,680
Xiaobei came to see me last night.

13
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,879
He wants to go back to Africa with us.

14
00:02:18,919 --> 00:02:20,280
We'd like to hear what you think.

15
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,080
Nonsense!

16
00:02:23,439 --> 00:02:24,800
Xiaobei works for Zhong'an.

17
00:02:25,639 --> 00:02:27,360
He can't just go wherever he pleases.

18
00:02:28,879 --> 00:02:29,680
Let go of me!

19
00:02:29,919 --> 00:02:31,680
Dad, why won't you let me go?

20
00:02:31,879 --> 00:02:33,159
Eavesdropping at the door?

21
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,319
Who taught you that?

22
00:02:36,639 --> 00:02:38,560
No, I... he just...

23
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:42,319
Old Qu, don't take the blame for him.

24
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,199
Dad!

25
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:44,319
You and Uncle Wei Tian

26
00:02:44,319 --> 00:02:45,800
went through life and death together!

27
00:02:46,039 --> 00:02:47,120
He's in grave danger now,

28
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:47,960
yet you don't even care!

29
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,400
That's a betrayal of trust, you know that?

30
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,039
Stop talking!

31
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:51,159
If you don't care, I will!

32
00:02:51,719 --> 00:02:53,080
If you don't want him as a friend, I do!

33
00:02:53,439 --> 00:02:54,680
I'll tell you the truth, Dad.

34
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,680
If you won't let me go,

35
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:56,599
from now on, you'll never deserve

36
00:02:56,599 --> 00:02:57,599
my respect!

37
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:01,159
Xiaobei, that's going a bit too far.

38
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:03,199
Everything was fine just a minute ago, right?

39
00:03:03,199 --> 00:03:04,120
What was fine?

40
00:03:04,719 --> 00:03:05,879
Which word of his didn't cross the line?

41
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:13,680
Get him out of here!

42
00:03:13,919 --> 00:03:15,319
Dad! Dad!

43
00:03:15,319 --> 00:03:15,479
Come on.

44
00:03:15,479 --> 00:03:15,759
Get out!

45
00:03:15,759 --> 00:03:16,479
Let's go.

46
00:03:17,319 --> 00:03:19,120
How can you face Uncle Wei doing this?

47
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,039
Dad!

48
00:03:23,479 --> 00:03:24,080
Let go of me!

49
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:26,879
Look, the kid is still young.

50
00:03:26,879 --> 00:03:28,319
He doesn't watch what he says.

51
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:30,120
Don't take it to heart.

52
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:31,360
Don't be angry, Mr. Xiang.

53
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:31,759
He's young and hot-headed.

54
00:03:31,759 --> 00:03:33,599
Right, can't help it. Takes after his dad.

55
00:03:35,919 --> 00:03:38,520
Old Qu, stop stirring the pot.

56
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:40,000
We're taking off now.

57
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,560
Take care. Let's go, let's go.

58
00:03:43,759 --> 00:03:44,879
Mr. Xiang, we're leaving.

59
00:03:44,879 --> 00:03:45,439
Talk to him calmly.

60
00:03:45,439 --> 00:03:47,759
Cool off, and reconsider Xiaobei's request.

61
00:03:47,759 --> 00:03:48,680
There's nothing to consider!

62
00:03:49,199 --> 00:03:50,199
Think about it, really.

63
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:51,319
Let's go, let's go.

64
00:04:13,159 --> 00:04:14,719
Call me when you get there.

65
00:04:15,159 --> 00:04:16,319
Stay in touch.

66
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:17,639
Okay.

67
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:19,160
I'm guessing...

68
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,600
you'll be about two hours behind me.

69
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,160
Sounds about right.

70
00:04:29,439 --> 00:04:30,240
All right.

71
00:04:30,879 --> 00:04:31,720
What is it?

72
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,199
More than two hours.

73
00:04:34,959 --> 00:04:36,279
Okay, I'm heading out.

74
00:04:36,839 --> 00:04:37,639
Goodbye.

75
00:04:44,399 --> 00:04:45,720
Xiaobei! Xiaobei!

76
00:04:46,519 --> 00:04:47,959
You're not really going to see your dad, are you?

77
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,000
Third time's the charm.

78
00:04:50,079 --> 00:04:52,120
I refuse to believe my dad would just abandon Wei Tian.

79
00:04:52,279 --> 00:04:53,199
Don't worry.

80
00:04:53,639 --> 00:04:55,680
Mr. Xiang already sent Helen to back up Wei Tian.

81
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:57,439
Besides, Rosie and Captain...

82
00:04:57,439 --> 00:04:58,279
just headed over too, didn't they?

83
00:04:58,279 --> 00:04:59,120
That's different.

84
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,199
Besides, is Wei Tian the kind of guy...

85
00:05:01,199 --> 00:05:02,879
who backs down when things get tough?

86
00:05:03,839 --> 00:05:04,959
When you get chewed out in a minute,

87
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,439
don't blame me for not stopping you.

88
00:05:06,439 --> 00:05:07,519
What are you afraid of?

89
00:05:07,959 --> 00:05:08,959
They've all gone to the front line.

90
00:05:08,959 --> 00:05:10,000
It's just the two of us left now.

91
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,360
Don't be a coward.

92
00:05:14,839 --> 00:05:16,319
Who's a coward?

93
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,199
Here, have some tea.

94
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:28,959
Come on in.

95
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:34,600
Dad.

96
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:37,879
You knew I was outside all along?

97
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:39,759
We've been waiting for you.

98
00:05:41,079 --> 00:05:43,519
Thought you'd rush over first thing in the morning.

99
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:46,600
Not bad. You managed to keep your cool.

100
00:05:47,759 --> 00:05:49,360
Unlike a certain uncle of yours.

101
00:05:50,839 --> 00:05:51,920
Drink your tea. Drink your tea.

102
00:05:54,519 --> 00:05:56,519
Speak up. What brings you here?

103
00:05:58,279 --> 00:06:00,519
I want to apply to return to the African branch.

104
00:06:02,879 --> 00:06:04,199
Since you can't sit still,

105
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,920
I happen to have a mission for you.

106
00:06:10,639 --> 00:06:12,000
Come on, Dad!

107
00:06:12,639 --> 00:06:14,160
It's an absolute emergency in Africa right now!

108
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:16,120
How could I have time for another mission?

109
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:17,879
Take it easy.

110
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,120
Hear your dad out first.

111
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:21,680
Take a look before you say anything.

112
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:43,439
Dad, you mean you want me to lead a team

113
00:06:43,439 --> 00:06:44,279
to Antilocaris

114
00:06:44,279 --> 00:06:45,439
to protect Plato Hotel?

115
00:06:45,439 --> 00:06:47,120
Wei Tian is in danger.

116
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,959
I understand how you feel.

117
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:51,160
However, our Zhong'an Group

118
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:54,199
must have a legitimate and lawful reason

119
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:56,120
to enter Antilocaris.

120
00:06:56,199 --> 00:06:58,120
Plato Hotel's plea for help right now

121
00:06:58,279 --> 00:06:59,720
is the perfect opportunity.

122
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:02,240
I've officially hired your Uncle Qu

123
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:05,000
as a guide to go back to Africa with you.

124
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:06,680
Any questions?

125
00:07:06,959 --> 00:07:07,759
None, sir.

126
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:11,639
Dad, turns out you never forgot

127
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:13,079
those old friends of yours.

128
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:14,560
Of course I haven't.

129
00:07:16,319 --> 00:07:17,720
Xiaobei is coming with me this time,

130
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,120
so don't you worry.

131
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,800
I promise to keep him in my sight at all times.

132
00:07:26,319 --> 00:07:27,199
Once in Africa,

133
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:28,920
your first priority is

134
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,959
the security of Plato Hotel.

135
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,600
Consider it done!

136
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:34,000
I'm not finished yet.

137
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:37,759
Security at Plato is only part of it.

138
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,720
You must coordinate with Wei Tian,

139
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,279
helping him and backing him up.

140
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:44,240
I'll await your news at headquarters.

141
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:44,879
Yes, sir!

142
00:07:44,879 --> 00:07:45,720
And another thing.

143
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,680
When we head out later,

144
00:07:47,959 --> 00:07:49,120
pack up all your dad's tea

145
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:50,560
for me to take with me.

146
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:51,879
Yes, sir.

147
00:07:55,079 --> 00:07:57,000
I'm hooked. It's good tea.

148
00:08:11,079 --> 00:08:12,040
But to be honest,

149
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,319
I really don't want you to go.

150
00:08:13,519 --> 00:08:14,360
Especially

151
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:16,279
to a place like Antilocaris.

152
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:23,199
The Silent Protectors are gone now,

153
00:08:23,279 --> 00:08:24,560
and Wei Tian is out of reach.

154
00:08:25,079 --> 00:08:26,600
Are you sure you want to go?

155
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,800
I only know four Silent Protectors.

156
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:34,120
Two have safely returned home,

157
00:08:34,679 --> 00:08:37,519
and one has stayed in Antilocaris.

158
00:08:37,919 --> 00:08:38,720
Yes,

159
00:08:39,159 --> 00:08:40,960
but Wei Tian can't be reached at all.

160
00:08:47,519 --> 00:08:49,559
I believe I'll still see him.

161
00:08:49,879 --> 00:08:50,720
Oh, you...

162
00:08:52,919 --> 00:08:53,919
What if in the end,

163
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:57,279
you're left in deep pain

164
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,720
and utterly tormented?

165
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:02,960
If I don't face it myself,

166
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,159
I won't be happy either.

167
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,440
I'd rather face it head-on.

168
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,919
Through all the grief and pain,

169
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:09,120
there might still be moments of joy.

170
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:12,519
You're such a silly girl.

171
00:09:14,399 --> 00:09:15,559
Just support me, okay?

172
00:09:18,159 --> 00:09:20,120
And what if in the end,

173
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:21,519
you're the only one left?

174
00:09:22,399 --> 00:09:24,120
Then what if,

175
00:09:24,639 --> 00:09:27,480
in the end, I'm heartbroken?

176
00:09:27,679 --> 00:09:28,919
You'll comfort me, right?

177
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:30,039
No.

178
00:09:31,519 --> 00:09:33,360
I'll definitely tell you that you had it coming.

179
00:09:34,639 --> 00:09:35,440
Fine.

180
00:09:37,679 --> 00:09:40,080
Once you're there, take good care of yourself.

181
00:09:40,639 --> 00:09:41,519
I'll wait for you to come back.

182
00:09:42,799 --> 00:09:43,600
Boss Zuo,

183
00:09:43,919 --> 00:09:45,720
take good care of your military club,

184
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,200
and wait for our triumphant return.

185
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,000
You bet.

186
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:49,679
I'll await your triumphant return.

187
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:51,240
Don't just focus on making money

188
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:52,480
and neglect your training.

189
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,519
Or you might not graduate.

190
00:09:54,159 --> 00:09:54,960
Don't worry.

191
00:09:59,759 --> 00:10:00,559
Wishing you all the best.

192
00:10:00,559 --> 00:10:01,279
All right.

193
00:10:02,759 --> 00:10:04,519
Okay, let's head out.

194
00:10:15,759 --> 00:10:18,360
Captain, please bring them back safely.

195
00:10:18,519 --> 00:10:20,519
Don't worry. Wait for us to come back.

196
00:10:21,399 --> 00:10:22,279
We'll wait for you to come back.

197
00:11:37,039 --> 00:11:37,840
Thank you.

198
00:12:08,639 --> 00:12:09,480
Damn it.

199
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,120
Hey, come here.

200
00:12:13,279 --> 00:12:14,080
What's wrong?

201
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,559
What's the matter with my car?

202
00:12:17,559 --> 00:12:18,720
Why won't it start?

203
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:19,480
Your car?

204
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,120
Yes.

205
00:12:20,279 --> 00:12:21,360
Is there a problem?

206
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,480
I already put gas in it.

207
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:24,000
So why won't it start?

208
00:12:24,279 --> 00:12:26,000
What exactly do you want me to do?

209
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,200
Help me fix it.

210
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:27,960
Fix it?

211
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:28,720
Of course.

212
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:31,279
That's not my job.

213
00:12:31,279 --> 00:12:32,080
I'll pay you.

214
00:12:32,159 --> 00:12:32,879
Sorry, no can do.

215
00:12:32,879 --> 00:12:33,720
Don't walk away. Help me fix it!

216
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:34,679
I really can't fix it.

217
00:12:34,679 --> 00:12:35,360
I'll give you money!

218
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,559
It's not about money.

219
00:12:36,559 --> 00:12:37,399
Fix it for me!

220
00:12:37,399 --> 00:12:38,240
Good grief, who is this guy?

221
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,519
Help me fix my car!

222
00:12:39,879 --> 00:12:41,080
Why is this happening?

223
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:42,399
Damn it!

224
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:43,679
Need some help?

225
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,360
You know how to fix cars?

226
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:56,120
This is a journey of forging ahead.

227
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:58,200
In the history of Antilocaris,

228
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,720
there is no precedent.

229
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:02,519
If we fail to find the right direction,

230
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:06,399
our nation's progress will surely be hindered.

231
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:10,080
Only through relentless reform

232
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:14,120
can we break free from poverty and disease.

233
00:13:14,879 --> 00:13:17,600
This is the journey to transform our destiny.

234
00:13:17,879 --> 00:13:19,120
Walter has already

235
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:22,279
joined forces with terrorists.

236
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:26,080
We must not give in to them,

237
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:28,080
nor believe their rumors.

238
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:31,919
Try it now.

239
00:13:41,519 --> 00:13:43,759
Awesome! I shall bestow a reward upon you.

240
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,279
What did you say? "Bestow a reward"?

241
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,200
What's your name?

242
00:13:50,519 --> 00:13:51,519
I'm Rosie.

243
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:54,360
How is your Chinese so good?

244
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:56,080
Naturally.

245
00:13:56,279 --> 00:13:57,480
My country and China

246
00:13:57,480 --> 00:13:59,799
have traded together for many years.

247
00:14:01,279 --> 00:14:02,080
Get in.

248
00:14:02,559 --> 00:14:03,320
Sorry.

249
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,360
I don't just get into strangers' cars.

250
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,960
In my capacity as Crown Prince of Libania,

251
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:09,919
I command you to get in.

252
00:14:10,399 --> 00:14:11,200
What?

253
00:14:12,559 --> 00:14:13,759
Just get in.

254
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,080
I mean no harm.

255
00:14:15,279 --> 00:14:17,399
I just want to thank you properly.

256
00:14:18,159 --> 00:14:19,639
Then why lie to me

257
00:14:19,639 --> 00:14:21,080
and claim to be the neighboring Crown Prince?

258
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:22,399
I didn't lie to you!

259
00:14:23,879 --> 00:14:25,600
Libania's investiture ceremony

260
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,279
isn't until next month.

261
00:14:27,639 --> 00:14:29,200
Besides, the Crown Prince's identity

262
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,720
has never been made public.

263
00:14:32,679 --> 00:14:33,720
Look...

264
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,320
I snuck out.

265
00:14:40,879 --> 00:14:44,120
Ever since they announced the ceremony,

266
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,240
they haven't let me go outside.

267
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:47,519
It's already been six months.

268
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:50,919
Fine, I believe you.

269
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:54,120
Still, even if you hadn't run into me,

270
00:14:54,279 --> 00:14:55,919
they'd have come to pick you up soon.

271
00:14:59,279 --> 00:15:00,080
What's this?

272
00:15:00,639 --> 00:15:03,120
A GPS tracker installed on your car.

273
00:15:03,879 --> 00:15:05,279
They're actually tracking me?!

274
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,559
How could they ever feel safe

275
00:15:08,559 --> 00:15:10,919
letting you sneak out and drive alone?

276
00:15:11,519 --> 00:15:12,399
Take my advice:

277
00:15:12,399 --> 00:15:14,720
stay in the car and wait for them to pick you up.

278
00:15:16,679 --> 00:15:18,320
Rosie, you're not allowed to leave!

279
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:20,720
The car is already fixed.

280
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:21,960
Why do you want me to stay here?

281
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:22,799
You... just stay right here

282
00:15:22,799 --> 00:15:24,120
and wait with me until they get here.

283
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:25,200
Sorry,

284
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:26,919
but I really have urgent business to attend to.

285
00:15:28,799 --> 00:15:30,679
Please just stay here with me until they arrive!

286
00:15:30,759 --> 00:15:32,519
To repay you for fixing my car,

287
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:34,480
I'll grant you one request,

288
00:15:35,279 --> 00:15:38,399
and then give you a car, too!

289
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:45,080
We are currently in a period of reform.

290
00:15:46,519 --> 00:15:49,399
Factions on all sides refuse to cooperate.

291
00:15:49,799 --> 00:15:52,080
The reform has hit a bottleneck.

292
00:15:52,759 --> 00:15:54,799
Political factors are complex,

293
00:15:55,159 --> 00:15:58,480
and their impact on the reform

294
00:15:59,240 --> 00:16:00,720
cannot be ignored.

295
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:11,919
Help!

296
00:16:27,919 --> 00:16:29,840
Your Majesty, take off your clothes. Give them to me.

297
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:30,519
Okay.

298
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:36,960
Helen, protect the King.

299
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:37,639
Got it.

300
00:16:42,799 --> 00:16:43,600
Follow me.

301
00:16:44,159 --> 00:16:44,679
Come on. All right.

302
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:18,400
Wait, wait, wait!

303
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,319
Where are you going?

304
00:17:22,279 --> 00:17:23,599
Your Royal Highness...

305
00:17:25,039 --> 00:17:26,160
When on earth will your palace people

306
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:28,079
finally come pick you up?

307
00:17:28,599 --> 00:17:29,680
I told you before,

308
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:31,559
I have really urgent business.

309
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,400
I can't waste any more time here.

310
00:17:34,599 --> 00:17:36,519
I ran a bit far this time,

311
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,240
but don't worry.

312
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,680
They'll definitely come.

313
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:42,200
Besides, how can you leave on your own?

314
00:17:43,799 --> 00:17:46,079
There's a daily round-trip bus here.

315
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:48,720
Even though I can't head forward now,

316
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:50,920
the bus will be here shortly.

317
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,400
I can take it back first,

318
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:53,400
and come back tomorrow.

319
00:17:54,279 --> 00:17:55,680
I already promised you...

320
00:17:56,119 --> 00:17:57,000
a car,

321
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,359
if you wait here with me until they arrive.

322
00:17:59,839 --> 00:18:01,599
How could I break my word?

323
00:18:03,359 --> 00:18:04,559
Haven't you ever heard

324
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:06,359
that time is life?

325
00:18:07,799 --> 00:18:08,920
Because of this...

326
00:18:09,279 --> 00:18:11,039
groundless promise of yours,

327
00:18:11,039 --> 00:18:12,839
you've wasted half my day

328
00:18:12,839 --> 00:18:13,720
stuck waiting here.

329
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,200
I really can't afford this delay.

330
00:18:16,759 --> 00:18:19,200
Fine, we'll go together.

331
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:21,599
Go where?

332
00:18:23,279 --> 00:18:25,079
Aren't you heading that way?

333
00:18:25,759 --> 00:18:26,759
The people coming for me

334
00:18:26,759 --> 00:18:28,720
should be coming from that direction, too.

335
00:18:29,279 --> 00:18:30,359
Looking at you,

336
00:18:30,359 --> 00:18:31,960
you probably don't have much money on you.

337
00:18:32,799 --> 00:18:33,720
Tell you what,

338
00:18:34,319 --> 00:18:35,759
you should come with me.

339
00:18:36,119 --> 00:18:38,920
At least you won't be short on cash along the way.

340
00:18:40,799 --> 00:18:41,599
All right.

341
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:43,799
Seeing how sincere you are,

342
00:18:44,759 --> 00:18:45,680
I agree.

343
00:18:51,799 --> 00:18:53,480
You're driving way too slow!

344
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:54,799
Is it slow?

345
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,000
Pull over!

346
00:19:00,119 --> 00:19:01,400
I said pull over!

347
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:05,079
Pull over right this second!

348
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,519
What are you doing?

349
00:19:16,519 --> 00:19:17,519
What's your problem?

350
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:19,920
At this speed,

351
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,519
when will we ever get to Libania?

352
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:22,680
Get out.

353
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:23,960
Step out!

354
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:26,960
What do you think you're doing?

355
00:19:31,799 --> 00:19:32,599
Get in.

356
00:19:35,839 --> 00:19:36,640
Get in!

357
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:53,599
Slow down, this is my baby.

358
00:19:53,599 --> 00:19:54,759
Don't be so rough on it.

359
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:56,880
This is a sports car.

360
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:58,160
Treat it with some respect.

361
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:01,440
What, is there another problem?

362
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:02,359
Your Highness...

363
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:03,920
Obida.

364
00:20:06,279 --> 00:20:08,559
My name is Obida.

365
00:20:08,559 --> 00:20:09,319
Obida.

366
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:11,759
For the rest of the trip,

367
00:20:11,759 --> 00:20:13,519
you'd better just call me by my name.

368
00:20:13,759 --> 00:20:15,079
So we don't draw attention.

369
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:18,279
You're driving a car like this,

370
00:20:18,279 --> 00:20:19,559
and you're worried about drawing attention?

371
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:23,759
Tell me, did you have a nightmare just now?

372
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,480
How come the moment you woke up,

373
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,279
you're like a completely different person?

374
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:47,240
Boss.

375
00:20:49,119 --> 00:20:50,319
If the target dies,

376
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:52,319
wouldn't the game lose all its fun?

377
00:20:55,559 --> 00:20:56,960
I want him alive.

378
00:20:57,680 --> 00:20:59,079
I want to talk to him.

379
00:20:59,160 --> 00:20:59,960
Understood.

380
00:21:22,519 --> 00:21:24,000
Damn it, we're chasing the wrong person.

381
00:22:00,599 --> 00:22:02,039
You knew this would happen all along.

382
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,960
From the moment the port deal was signed,

383
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:11,240
you knew this would happen.

384
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:13,559
That's why you came to us.

385
00:22:14,319 --> 00:22:15,839
I did look into it.

386
00:22:15,839 --> 00:22:18,440
Zhong'an and Wei Tian were both in Antilocaris.

387
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:21,440
Aside from you, I had no better choice.

388
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:23,599
You're the best ones to protect me.

389
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Then why didn't you just hide?

390
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:28,359
Why choose to show your face at a time like this?

391
00:22:29,759 --> 00:22:32,680
Not only do I want to give a street speech,

392
00:22:32,799 --> 00:22:34,759
I want to appear before the entire nation.

393
00:22:34,839 --> 00:22:36,799
I want the people across the nation to know

394
00:22:36,799 --> 00:22:38,559
that their king is still here,

395
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:40,880
and hasn't fallen into the terrorists' hands.

396
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:43,079
Only then will everyone in the country know

397
00:22:43,079 --> 00:22:44,640
that these people didn't succeed,

398
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:47,279
and this country still has hope.

399
00:22:54,799 --> 00:22:56,359
The number you dialed

400
00:22:56,359 --> 00:22:57,720
is not answering at the moment.

401
00:22:57,799 --> 00:22:59,599
Please try again later.

402
00:22:59,599 --> 00:23:01,160
The number you dialed

403
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:02,519
is not answering at the moment.

404
00:23:02,599 --> 00:23:04,400
Please try again later.

405
00:23:04,759 --> 00:23:05,880
The number you dialed

406
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:07,160
is not answering at the moment.

407
00:23:12,559 --> 00:23:13,839
Your car is running out of gas.

408
00:23:15,119 --> 00:23:16,759
That attendant didn't fill it up.

409
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:19,400
Are you asking me?

410
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:24,640
Then let's find a gas station quickly.

411
00:23:50,559 --> 00:23:52,839
This could be local militants,

412
00:23:53,279 --> 00:23:55,759
or tribesmen who sabotaged it.

413
00:23:56,279 --> 00:23:58,200
Whoever trashed this place,

414
00:23:58,480 --> 00:23:59,319
the gas has definitely

415
00:23:59,319 --> 00:24:00,759
all been taken by now.

416
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:04,079
Our car's probably gonna break down halfway.

417
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:06,240
Are you sure your people are coming for you?

418
00:24:06,640 --> 00:24:07,759
By the looks of it,

419
00:24:08,079 --> 00:24:09,680
we have no choice but to push forward.

420
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:13,000
If the people coming to pick me up

421
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:14,839
have to cross a war zone,

422
00:24:15,799 --> 00:24:18,200
it'll be tough for them to get through.

423
00:24:19,440 --> 00:24:22,200
Leaving the car here isn't an option either.

424
00:24:24,440 --> 00:24:25,240
A train.

425
00:24:26,640 --> 00:24:28,000
I know that if we keep going,

426
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:29,160
there's a train station.

427
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:33,000
Should we switch to the train to get there?

428
00:24:33,319 --> 00:24:34,319
All right, let's go.

429
00:24:34,319 --> 00:24:34,599
Let's move.

430
00:24:34,599 --> 00:24:35,759
It beats breaking down on the way.

431
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:24,839
You really don't mind leaving your car here?

432
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:26,839
It has GPS anyway.

433
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:29,079
They'll bring my baby back.

434
00:25:31,079 --> 00:25:33,000
How did you know there was a train station here?

435
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:34,880
This railway...

436
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:37,559
is a strategic cooperation project between our two countries.

437
00:25:37,839 --> 00:25:40,200
We provided the Supedo government

438
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:42,400
with financial backing.

439
00:25:50,759 --> 00:25:52,440
Passengers, please cooperate.

440
00:25:53,319 --> 00:25:55,000
Have your passports and tickets ready.

441
00:25:55,319 --> 00:25:57,279
We're starting inspections now.

442
00:25:58,240 --> 00:25:59,039
My ticket...

443
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:08,039
I'm going over there for a moment.

444
00:26:08,839 --> 00:26:10,599
Are you worried about exposing

445
00:26:10,599 --> 00:26:11,880
your real identity?

446
00:26:14,559 --> 00:26:16,039
Go ahead. I was just guessing.

447
00:26:16,359 --> 00:26:19,079
Or you wouldn't have targeted me at the gas station.

448
00:26:20,400 --> 00:26:21,200
Hurry up and go.

449
00:26:22,160 --> 00:26:22,960
Go on.

450
00:26:34,920 --> 00:26:37,559
Hand over all your money!

451
00:26:39,599 --> 00:26:40,440
Hurry up!

452
00:26:42,200 --> 00:26:43,160
Hand it all over!

453
00:26:46,799 --> 00:26:48,039
We have to get out of here.

454
00:26:48,599 --> 00:26:49,480
Take it out, hurry!

455
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,440
Aren't they just after money?

456
00:26:52,599 --> 00:26:53,720
The last of my cash...

457
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:55,480
...was spent buying the tickets.

458
00:26:56,200 --> 00:26:57,640
The cash I have on me...

459
00:26:58,119 --> 00:26:59,680
...isn't accepted here.

460
00:27:01,079 --> 00:27:02,000
The things in here...

461
00:27:02,359 --> 00:27:03,880
...could blow my cover.

462
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:06,039
Get the money out!

463
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,200
Give it to me, hurry!

464
00:27:10,319 --> 00:27:12,599
You, open the bag and give me the money!

465
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:13,799
There's none left!

466
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:15,440
Everyone, hand over your money!

467
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:17,160
Give me the money!

468
00:27:17,319 --> 00:27:18,200
Don't shoot!

469
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:19,440
Okay, okay!

470
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:20,559
Hand over the money, now!

471
00:27:21,359 --> 00:27:22,279
Don't... don't kill me!

472
00:27:22,279 --> 00:27:24,759
Take out the money! Give it to me!

473
00:27:36,759 --> 00:27:37,200
Move.

474
00:27:39,400 --> 00:27:39,839
Move.

475
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:44,839
Move.

476
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:05,519
Hurry up

477
00:28:19,599 --> 00:28:20,599
Rosie! Rosie!

478
00:28:21,759 --> 00:28:22,640
I can't go on.

479
00:28:22,839 --> 00:28:24,799
I can't take it anymore, I'm exhausted!

480
00:28:30,039 --> 00:28:30,839
Good grief!

481
00:28:32,759 --> 00:28:33,559
Ow, ow, ow!

482
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:36,680
What are you doing?

483
00:28:36,680 --> 00:28:37,880
Come clean with me right now!

484
00:28:38,319 --> 00:28:39,119
Back on the train today,

485
00:28:39,119 --> 00:28:40,039
what on earth was going on?

486
00:28:40,039 --> 00:28:41,200
Who was looking for you?

487
00:28:42,079 --> 00:28:43,079
I'll talk! I'll talk!

488
00:28:43,079 --> 00:28:44,119
I... I'll tell—

489
00:28:44,119 --> 00:28:46,039
I'll tell you everything, all right?

490
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:55,480
The King hasn't been captured!

491
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:57,559
Everyone, look at this!

492
00:28:57,680 --> 00:28:58,839
Look at this, everyone!

493
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:01,519
Come look, everyone!

494
00:29:02,079 --> 00:29:03,079
What is this?

495
00:29:09,519 --> 00:29:10,359
It's the King!

496
00:29:10,720 --> 00:29:13,000
The King wasn't captured by the terrorists!

497
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:14,160
That's wonderful!

498
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:18,920
Where did all these come from?

499
00:29:18,920 --> 00:29:21,039
Arrest whoever is handing out flyers! Quick!

500
00:29:28,400 --> 00:29:29,440
Thank goodness!

501
00:29:31,759 --> 00:29:32,799
He's not dead!

502
00:29:33,440 --> 00:29:35,119
Thank you! Thank you, Your Majesty!

503
00:29:35,119 --> 00:29:36,079
Thank you, Your Majesty!

504
00:29:36,799 --> 00:29:38,160
Thank you! Thank you, Your Majesty!

505
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:39,440
Let's go!

506
00:29:40,039 --> 00:29:41,200
Move out!

507
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:55,240
Every country

508
00:29:55,599 --> 00:29:57,839
has discordant voices,

509
00:29:59,319 --> 00:30:00,839
and mine is no exception.

510
00:30:01,720 --> 00:30:04,240
The Kingdom of Supedo has been restless lately.

511
00:30:05,119 --> 00:30:07,079
There are constant wars between border tribes,

512
00:30:08,079 --> 00:30:10,640
and trouble seems to be brewing within the country.

513
00:30:13,599 --> 00:30:14,640
My father,

514
00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:17,759
to spare his people from disaster,

515
00:30:18,240 --> 00:30:21,559
has strictly maintained neutrality.

516
00:30:22,039 --> 00:30:25,240
He hasn't sent troops into Supedo

517
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:27,599
to take any action,

518
00:30:28,519 --> 00:30:29,759
nor has he provided

519
00:30:29,759 --> 00:30:32,079
the terrorists stirring up turmoil

520
00:30:32,079 --> 00:30:34,839
with any weapons

521
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:36,960
or financial support.

522
00:30:37,319 --> 00:30:39,559
He only reinforced border defenses.

523
00:30:44,119 --> 00:30:46,400
So you had no idea

524
00:30:46,400 --> 00:30:48,160
who those people on the train really were.

525
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:50,279
You were just afraid

526
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:51,680
they might be local

527
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:53,000
armed terrorists.

528
00:30:54,039 --> 00:30:55,200
You're right.

529
00:30:58,119 --> 00:30:59,839
You worried that once those terrorists

530
00:31:00,160 --> 00:31:01,680
found out who you were,

531
00:31:02,519 --> 00:31:03,839
they'd take you hostage

532
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:06,359
to force your father to support them.

533
00:31:07,839 --> 00:31:09,079
I'm sorry, Rosie,

534
00:31:10,279 --> 00:31:12,759
for dragging you into this danger with me.

535
00:31:14,839 --> 00:31:17,039
Didn't you want me to escort you home

536
00:31:17,599 --> 00:31:19,400
right from the start?

537
00:31:21,279 --> 00:31:23,400
The Silent Protectors really are impressive.

538
00:31:23,799 --> 00:31:24,839
I thought...

539
00:31:25,720 --> 00:31:26,519
you were still...

540
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:28,559
Actually,

541
00:31:28,599 --> 00:31:30,960
I was kept in the dark at first, too.

542
00:31:32,039 --> 00:31:32,799
It's just that,

543
00:31:32,799 --> 00:31:35,279
along the way, I realized

544
00:31:35,599 --> 00:31:38,400
you're not as simple as I thought.

545
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:42,039
How did you know I'm with the Silent Protectors?

546
00:31:43,279 --> 00:31:45,359
Actually, I've long known about

547
00:31:45,359 --> 00:31:47,359
the Silent Protectors in Antilocaris.

548
00:31:48,680 --> 00:31:50,519
I wanted to hire your team

549
00:31:50,519 --> 00:31:52,039
to work for our country long ago,

550
00:31:52,359 --> 00:31:54,400
but I could never track you down.

551
00:31:56,599 --> 00:31:58,960
Not until your base was bombed.

552
00:32:01,119 --> 00:32:03,160
I... I got hold of

553
00:32:03,160 --> 00:32:05,839
files on all of you.

554
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:08,200
There was barely any information,

555
00:32:09,880 --> 00:32:10,880
so I couldn't even tell

556
00:32:11,359 --> 00:32:13,200
whether it was real or fake.

557
00:32:14,119 --> 00:32:15,240
Looking at you now,

558
00:32:15,759 --> 00:32:17,559
your photo seems to have been genuine.

559
00:32:19,319 --> 00:32:20,119
Since

560
00:32:20,839 --> 00:32:23,039
you planned for me to escort you back,

561
00:32:23,079 --> 00:32:24,480
why didn't you just say so?

562
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:26,519
I didn't want you

563
00:32:26,519 --> 00:32:28,599
following me around like a clone,

564
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:30,799
just sticking by my side.

565
00:32:32,599 --> 00:32:34,440
That's the first time I've heard an excuse like that.

566
00:32:37,599 --> 00:32:39,559
What's the plan next?

567
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:41,039
We don't have a vehicle,

568
00:32:41,680 --> 00:32:42,839
or a tracker.

569
00:32:44,319 --> 00:32:46,599
But we still have the map.

570
00:32:47,960 --> 00:32:48,759
Where is it?

571
00:32:48,880 --> 00:32:49,839
Right here.

572
00:32:50,759 --> 00:32:53,839
Heading west from our current location,

573
00:32:54,119 --> 00:32:55,160
there's a tribe.

574
00:32:55,599 --> 00:32:56,640
It's quite remote,

575
00:32:57,119 --> 00:32:59,680
rarely touched by the war.

576
00:33:00,319 --> 00:33:02,640
How much longer do we have to walk to get there?

577
00:33:02,920 --> 00:33:05,599
We should be able to reach it by nightfall.

578
00:33:15,960 --> 00:33:16,759
Obida.

579
00:33:20,079 --> 00:33:20,960
Are you okay?

580
00:33:22,240 --> 00:33:22,880
I'm fine, I'm fine.

581
00:33:22,880 --> 00:33:23,480
How are you feeling?

582
00:33:23,480 --> 00:33:24,839
I just want something to eat.

583
00:33:25,839 --> 00:33:26,680
Go ahead and eat, then.

584
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:31,200
You didn't hurt yourself falling, right?

585
00:33:32,079 --> 00:33:32,880
Over there!

586
00:33:33,519 --> 00:33:34,319
Hurry!

587
00:33:34,480 --> 00:33:35,279
Quick!

588
00:33:35,559 --> 00:33:36,200
Don't move!

589
00:33:36,200 --> 00:33:37,039
Hand over your stuff!

590
00:33:38,319 --> 00:33:39,119
Wait!

591
00:33:39,960 --> 00:33:40,759
Don't move!

592
00:33:41,279 --> 00:33:42,240
We're friendly!

593
00:33:42,240 --> 00:33:42,960
Put your hands down!

594
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:44,759
We'll give you all the food, okay?

595
00:33:47,359 --> 00:33:49,559
All of it. We'll give you all of it!

596
00:33:49,960 --> 00:33:50,759
Look, look!

597
00:33:51,839 --> 00:33:52,839
Look, take it!

598
00:33:53,160 --> 00:33:53,960
See?

599
00:33:54,880 --> 00:33:56,839
I have nothing left. Nothing!

600
00:33:56,839 --> 00:33:57,519
Give it all to us!

601
00:33:57,960 --> 00:33:58,720
Is there any more?

602
00:33:58,720 --> 00:34:00,119
I gave you everything! There's no more!

603
00:34:00,119 --> 00:34:00,599
Hand it all over!

604
00:34:00,599 --> 00:34:01,160
Take everything out!

605
00:34:01,160 --> 00:34:02,160
There's nothing left!

606
00:34:02,160 --> 00:34:02,599
Hurry up!

607
00:34:02,599 --> 00:34:03,480
I've given you everything!

608
00:34:04,559 --> 00:34:05,359
See?

609
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:55,199
Don't shoot! Don't shoot!

610
00:34:55,199 --> 00:34:56,119
It's me! It's me!

611
00:34:56,119 --> 00:34:58,000
Don't misunderstand! It's just me!

612
00:34:58,920 --> 00:35:00,280
Why are you still awake?

613
00:35:00,960 --> 00:35:02,360
Good thing I didn't sleep.

614
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:03,679
We're in trouble.

615
00:35:04,480 --> 00:35:06,880
I just overheard the people outside saying

616
00:35:07,360 --> 00:35:08,960
someone recognized who I am,

617
00:35:09,400 --> 00:35:12,599
and wants to hand me over to Supedo terrorists

618
00:35:13,119 --> 00:35:14,480
in exchange for food!

619
00:35:57,559 --> 00:35:58,239
Let's go.

620
00:35:58,239 --> 00:35:58,880
All right.

621
00:36:05,920 --> 00:36:07,840
I don't think they'd chase us out here.

622
00:36:08,679 --> 00:36:10,960
Have you been to this tribe before?

623
00:36:11,599 --> 00:36:13,679
I was here three years ago.

624
00:36:14,400 --> 00:36:17,400
An epidemic broke out here.

625
00:36:17,920 --> 00:36:19,760
Once we found out about it,

626
00:36:20,320 --> 00:36:23,039
we made sure to bring them

627
00:36:23,679 --> 00:36:26,039
clean food and medicine.

628
00:36:27,119 --> 00:36:28,360
For them to repay our kindness like this...

629
00:36:28,360 --> 00:36:29,800
it's really crossing the line.

630
00:36:30,039 --> 00:36:31,000
Maybe they

631
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:33,199
just want out of their current situation.

632
00:36:35,079 --> 00:36:37,400
Do you think we should take a break?

633
00:36:38,039 --> 00:36:38,840
You tired?

634
00:36:39,039 --> 00:36:39,840
Exhausted.

635
00:36:40,599 --> 00:36:41,639
Here's my take:

636
00:36:42,280 --> 00:36:43,519
we can rest during the day,

637
00:36:43,519 --> 00:36:46,239
and tonight, while it's cooler,

638
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:47,199
hurry and push forward.

639
00:36:48,400 --> 00:36:49,840
If we still can't find water,

640
00:36:50,119 --> 00:36:51,480
with our current stamina,

641
00:36:51,920 --> 00:36:53,800
we won't make it eight kilometers in daylight.

642
00:36:56,039 --> 00:36:59,000
Luckily, I grabbed this when we left.

643
00:37:40,320 --> 00:37:41,039
There's water.

644
00:37:41,039 --> 00:37:41,840
Be careful.

645
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:45,480
This well probably belongs to someone.

646
00:37:46,119 --> 00:37:47,840
You mean whoever dug it?

647
00:37:48,599 --> 00:37:49,400
Not necessarily.

648
00:37:49,719 --> 00:37:51,599
But definitely someone armed.

649
00:37:52,119 --> 00:37:53,880
Let's just wait here.

650
00:38:10,039 --> 00:38:10,840
Come on.

651
00:38:13,079 --> 00:38:13,880
Don't move!

652
00:38:15,760 --> 00:38:16,800
This is my well.

653
00:38:17,199 --> 00:38:20,039
Drinking my water comes at a price.

654
00:38:21,599 --> 00:38:22,360
Are you

655
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:24,199
people from Supedo crossing the border?

656
00:38:24,719 --> 00:38:27,000
I'm not drinking your water for free.

657
00:38:27,320 --> 00:38:28,559
I'm asking you a question!

658
00:38:28,599 --> 00:38:29,639
Who are you?

659
00:38:29,840 --> 00:38:31,039
Where did you come from?

660
00:38:31,679 --> 00:38:34,480
Nice shotgun you've got there.

661
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:42,000
You know about guns?

662
00:38:42,719 --> 00:38:44,559
I don't have time to chat with you.

663
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:47,039
Hand over whatever valuables you have, now!

664
00:38:47,679 --> 00:38:49,639
That's what you owe me for the water.

665
00:38:50,400 --> 00:38:50,960
Here.

666
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:51,719
Give me money!

667
00:38:55,719 --> 00:38:57,079
This isn't nearly enough!

668
00:38:57,119 --> 00:38:59,239
Don't try to cheat me. Now get lost!

669
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:14,679
Let go of me!

670
00:39:14,719 --> 00:39:15,400
This is my well!

671
00:39:15,400 --> 00:39:16,400
That's probably

672
00:39:16,400 --> 00:39:18,440
the most he's ever been paid for water.

673
00:39:19,079 --> 00:39:20,159
Let me go!

674
00:39:23,199 --> 00:39:24,719
If we weren't in such a rush to leave,

675
00:39:24,719 --> 00:39:26,159
I wouldn't let you off so easily.

676
00:39:27,079 --> 00:39:27,800
See ya.

677
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:28,800
Don't leave!

678
00:39:28,840 --> 00:39:29,639
Goodbye.

679
00:39:29,719 --> 00:39:30,760
Let me go!

680
00:39:30,760 --> 00:39:31,239
Let's move.

681
00:39:31,239 --> 00:39:32,400
Let go of me!

682
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:39,800
The oasis is right up ahead.

683
00:39:40,199 --> 00:39:40,960
You've been here before?

684
00:39:40,960 --> 00:39:42,000
Of course I have.

685
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:44,400
And I've got good news, too.

686
00:39:44,679 --> 00:39:45,559
Now that we're here,

687
00:39:45,559 --> 00:39:47,400
I know where we need to head next.

688
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:48,880
Where's that?

689
00:39:49,719 --> 00:39:51,239
Further west,

690
00:39:51,920 --> 00:39:53,079
there's a safe house.

691
00:39:53,480 --> 00:39:55,440
A married couple runs the place.

692
00:39:56,159 --> 00:39:57,280
Once we get there,

693
00:39:57,280 --> 00:39:58,840
we'll have working communications.

694
00:39:59,559 --> 00:40:00,400
How much further?

695
00:40:01,480 --> 00:40:04,000
About a two-hour walk.

696
00:40:04,719 --> 00:40:06,599
That means before it gets dark,

697
00:40:06,599 --> 00:40:07,679
we can definitely make it.

698
00:40:07,800 --> 00:40:08,760
We should be able to.

699
00:40:08,920 --> 00:40:09,519
Let's go.

700
00:40:09,519 --> 00:40:10,159
Move out.

701
00:40:38,719 --> 00:40:41,000
Is this the safe house you mentioned?

702
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:42,679
Yes.

703
00:40:43,639 --> 00:40:45,039
It's not a bad spot.

704
00:40:46,480 --> 00:40:47,639
Before we go in,

705
00:40:47,679 --> 00:40:50,239
shouldn't we have a code word with them?

706
00:40:50,599 --> 00:40:51,960
Do you still have a gun on you?

707
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:54,559
Yeah, but I'm low on ammo.

708
00:40:57,760 --> 00:41:00,159
Something might've happened to the safe house manager.

709
00:41:12,320 --> 00:41:13,239
Something's definitely wrong.

710
00:41:14,320 --> 00:41:15,559
If it were safe,

711
00:41:15,719 --> 00:41:17,159
every four hours,

712
00:41:17,159 --> 00:41:19,880
he'd change the cloth strip on the railing.

713
00:41:20,840 --> 00:41:22,599
At six in the morning, it's blue.

714
00:41:23,079 --> 00:41:26,000
At ten in the morning, it's yellow.

715
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:27,400
At two in the afternoon,

716
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:29,400
they change it to green.

717
00:41:29,920 --> 00:41:31,880
At six in the evening, it's red.

718
00:41:33,719 --> 00:41:36,280
Normally, it should be red by now.

719
00:41:36,599 --> 00:41:38,480
How did you tell something was off?

720
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:40,760
The blinds.

721
00:41:41,360 --> 00:41:43,599
The blinds were closed just a moment ago.

722
00:41:44,079 --> 00:41:45,360
Now the angle they're open at

723
00:41:45,480 --> 00:41:47,400
allows someone inside to watch outside.

724
00:41:50,480 --> 00:41:51,480
So what do we do?

725
00:41:52,320 --> 00:41:53,519
If we abandon this place,

726
00:41:53,519 --> 00:41:54,440
I don't know

727
00:41:54,840 --> 00:41:56,000
how much longer we'll have to wait

728
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:58,320
for the people coming for us

729
00:41:58,320 --> 00:41:59,400
to pick us up.

730
00:42:01,239 --> 00:42:02,800
Why should we abandon it?
